  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_402653eb9bb1468b83454f686c200e5b",
      "statement": "Client routes are defined in `src/app/app.routes.ts`: public auth screens are top-level routes, all authenticated screens are children of a `Shell` component at `path: ''` protected by `authGuard`, and the catch-all `**` redirects to `''` so unknown URLs land on the authenticated home (or trigger the login redirect).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.routes.ts#L25-L111",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:730f8400c0ab587972a95278db48c7d5c59085140e34c9dc50a9d73b88377f87:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2d464ee3d5934e9ba2f56b2dc9137434",
      "statement": "Feature flags from `environment.features` conditionally include client routes by spreading conditional arrays into the routes table: `emailRegistration || oauthLogin` includes `auth/signup`; `emailRegistration` alone includes `auth/verify`; `passwordReset` includes `auth/forgot-password` and `auth/reset-password`; `teamInvitations` includes the dual invitation paths. A disabled flag removes both the route and the corresponding UI entry points (login/signup links and forms).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.routes.ts#L21-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ffd7f80753bf06021e9a128474026f887efb76cc54d46f0945dcab17e9683bd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/auth/login/login.html#L9-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:696e45aa68b74b555239468726ff3de8d9e70dbf7a4197afd79722f6d200a884:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/auth/signup/signup.html#L15-L22",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d2759456a49f6a70a43ce8ea3512e8258e00706df10bd9a398353ba3ee435e31:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cf61b8a26d624177b89d17b2996988f4",
      "statement": "The feature flags must match the Sign-up Mgmt Features toggles of the linked Ulabase service: a feature that is off server-side returns 403 to unauthenticated users, so the app must not offer routes or UI for it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/environments/environment.ts#L8-L17",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8c3fa77f06741a06457709d436d2adee921e0812e175ca965979700d23f358ef:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_836068175dd84958864de666d0466801",
      "statement": "`authGuard` (on the shell root) runs `checkSession()` and redirects to `/auth/login` when no user is found; `publicGuard` (on every auth screen) redirects signed-in users away from auth pages into the app. Guard evaluation is what normally loads the session: `checkSession()` also loads team memberships as a side effect.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://PORTING.md#L75-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:428eea0d9d6778967d11f1769efb66081e7ca8cae33a1bb2df88619a6a214f7b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.routes.ts#L25-L83",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f724df363007086c028cfaca773eb763d6439100e2b40595c659aaf886ad7add:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_802201849d4c4b10bd6efbea017f793e",
      "statement": "Under `teamInvitations`, the same `Accept` component is registered at two paths — `auth/activate` (linked from the invitation email for new users) and `invitations/accept` (for existing users) — both deliberately unguarded because the invitee may be signed out, signed in, or have no account yet.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.routes.ts#L68-L79",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:369d4385687df27708dc41964b8a3bfe5310047501a067408b55c50197c7cfe8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bdfcc2a016b542ddb1006b1542e8a2be",
      "statement": "Because the invitation route has no guard, the `Accept` component restores the session by hand: it calls `auth.checkSession()` whenever `getToken()` is truthy, then fetches the invitation via `getInvitation(email, token)` and offers three outcomes — `activate()` for new users, `login()` + `acceptInvite()` for existing users, or redirect into the app if the invitation is already used and a session exists.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/pages/invitations/accept/accept.ts#L42-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31fc809c374c78952b0c3a4169ce62c8eb8d3a0cf960951b28347b933b09d8c9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fc42562eb9204a6c86614d8dbcb04bad",
      "statement": "`src/app/app.routes.server.ts` must mirror the conditional client routes in `app.routes.ts`: every `ServerRoute` entry must match an actual client route or Angular SSR route extraction fails the build. The same `environment.features` flags gate the same conditional blocks on both sides.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.routes.server.ts#L4-L59",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:21e332418e1197ee78c2e660b5b37c3f675aabcafb76557eb61792232782d284:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_705fdc7d98124c4ca9559526c5588323",
      "statement": "Both invitation paths (`auth/activate`, `invitations/accept`) use `RenderMode.Client` because the `Accept` component makes live API calls on init and reads browser-side session state. The authenticated shell is also `RenderMode.Client` because the bearer token lives in `localStorage`. Public auth pages are `Prerender` except `auth/verify`, which is `Client` (calls `verify()` via API then shows the result).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.routes.server.ts#L11-L57",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d043b8e8122bb2f26ebd0c8e83d7dc6021f77c1ce378b6958f50f7a56c53ceac:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c15c7dabab3546d4b0dc03bf8769cdfc",
      "statement": "`AppTitleStrategy` extends Angular's `TitleStrategy` and appends a fixed suffix: the document title becomes `\"<Route title> · Ulabase Starter\"`, or just `Ulabase Starter` when no route title is set. The strategy is installed in `app.config.ts` via `{ provide: TitleStrategy, useClass: AppTitleStrategy }`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.config.ts#L25-L25",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c78ca43499657839882a147f83ae3e682211992a94c0e0e18200eb0c1f1bc99:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.routes.ts#L7-L18",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe038666f6358f404523fe62a9c4ebe74f3c295cf161c70fc4d95c8b2fea82e4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_87841be972d54a018b6d208ebae056a1",
      "statement": "When `apiUrl` is missing or not a valid Ulabase URL, `app.config.ts` registers an empty route table (`activeRoutes = []`) so no guard ever runs against a missing backend. This prevents `authGuard`'s `checkSession()` from producing a confusing network error on first run.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/app/app.config.ts#L12-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77e3870255533a0ab372548acc8a95c1bbbfb8286afd1e15976313f5de99fee4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8cbf029afafb4bbe8712d051b4870fc1",
      "statement": "Feature flags gate UI in templates: `login.html` hides the OAuth buttons (`oauthLogin`), the forgot-password link (`passwordReset`), and the signup link (`emailRegistration || oauthLogin`); `signup.html` hides the OAuth buttons (`oauthLogin`) and the email registration form (`emailRegistration`). The home-page capability list still shows disabled features but marks them `off` — it is a status display, not an entry point.",
